3. Understanding of local postion and World postion ---------- 
AtomContainer (World Position)
    └── Nucleus (local 0,0,0)
         └── Ring (local 0,0,0)
             └── Electrons (local positions around the ring)

-- > child.transform.localPosition = new Vector3(0, 2, 0);
      -- it means chikd is 2 unit above the parents  ;
Note : 
 -> When localPosition = Vector3.zero, the child sits at the parent's center, not the world's center.
